                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">Microsoft Azure – Create Project in Azure Devops using Agile Process
Agile Process is used when a team uses Agile planning methods, including Scrum, and used to track
development and test activities separately. Agile provides different work items using these work
items you can track different types of work [ features, user stories, and tasks] based on Agile
principles and values.

Step 1: Go to Azure DevOps Portal and Sign in with your Microsoft Account. You will also need to
choose your Organization (If you don’t have an organization create one)




Step 2: Create Project with Agile Process in Azure Devops
•   Click on New Project button on the top right corner.




•   Enter information into the Panel that opens:

        o   Enter the name of your project.

        o   Project name can’t contain special characters such as / : \ ~ &amp; % ; @@ &#x27; &quot; ? &lt; &gt; | # $ * }
            { , + = [ ], can&#x27;t begin with an underscore and must be 64 or fewer characters.

        o   Enter the description this field is optional.

        o   Choose the visibility of either public or private.

                o   Public: With public visibility, anyone on the internet has the right to view
                    your project.

                o   Private: With private visibility, only people to whom you give access can view
                    your project.

                o   Choose the right version control.

                o   Choose the Work Item Process.
Step 3: Click the Create button. Navigated to Welcome page. You can choose one of the options
display on the welcome screen to continue.</pre>
